<h3>Concept</h3>
<p>Our initial concept was a tower defence where the paths
 generate randomly and branch out into multiple paths as it
 goes further into the game. Our team was split between 4
 programmers. I was to create the procedural pathing and
 the UI for the main menu.</p>

<h3>Process</h3>
<p>I began first with a sprite sheet of all possible paths that
 a hexagonal path could take. Unity has a built-in tile generator
 for this need called a Rule Tile.</p>
 
<p>However, I knew that I wanted paths to be able to be
 beside each other but not be connected. The way Unity's
 method works is by just checking if its neighbours are
 the same type of tile, not checking if it is on the same
 path or not. This would lead to a weird grid pathing.
 So I first began with having to make my own system.</p>

